.TH DEEPIRI\-TOMBSTONE 1 2026\-06\-19 "deepiri\-tombstone 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deepiri\-tombstone \- multi\-language post\-training evaluation harness for Ollama
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deepiri\-tombstone
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deepiri\-tombstone
is an end\-to-end evaluation harness for Ollama models. The pipeline
tokenizes prompts (Forth), builds HTTP requests (BCPL), invokes the
Ollama API (C), parses JSON responses (AWK), scores results (Fortran),
and maintains an audit ledger (COBOL). Each stage has a native compiler
path and a POSIX fallback script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-host \fI\,ADDR\/\fR
Ollama server address (default: 127.0.0.1:11434).
Overrides \fB\(scDEEPIRI_TOMBSTONE_HOST\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-model \fI\,NAME\/\fR
Model name (default: llama3.2).
Overrides \fB\(scDEEPIRI_TOMBSTONE_MODEL\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-fixture \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to fixture file with prompts.
Default: fixtures/eval_prompts.txt.
.TP
.B \-\-output \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write audit output to FILE.
Default: stdout.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEEPIRI_TOMBSTONE_HOST
Ollama server address (default: 127.0.0.1:11434).
.TP
.B DEEPIRI_TOMBSTONE_MODEL
Default model name (default: llama3.2).
.TP
.B DEEPIRI_TOMBSTONE_FIXTURE
Default fixture file path.
.TP
.B DEEPIRI_TOMBSTONE_OUTPUT
Set to \fBjson\fR for JSON output from fallback scripts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B fixtures/eval_prompts.txt
Standard evaluation prompts with keyword pass criteria.
.TP
.B fixtures/benchmark_prompts.txt
Longer prompts for throughput benchmarking.
.TP
.B fixtures/edge_cases.txt
Edge cases: empty prompts, special characters, unicode.
.TP
.B fixtures/stress_prompts.txt
Stress test prompts for high\-volume evaluation.
.TP
.B reports/
Output directory for audit logs and evaluation reports.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
All evaluations passed.
.TP
1
One or more evaluations failed.
.TP
2
Configuration or dependency error.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Team\-Deepiri/deepiri\-tombstone/issues\fR.
.SH AUTHOR
Team Deepiri
.SH SEE ALSO
